raw.opening_A:
{
"explanation": "In these assays, Orava spores stay dormant until they receive one specific cue, followed by sustained moisture. Moisture alone does nothing, so a moisture-only cohort stays dormant at the five-day endpoint. The cue that breaks dormancy here is the smoke-derived chemical exposure. Once spores have had that exposure and then 48 hours of wet conditions, dormancy breaks and they germinate by the endpoint. Two full freeze-thaw cycles are a different treatment. Because these cohorts start equally dormant, with permissive nutrients, light, temperature, substrate and viability, freeze-thaw followed by moisture supplies no cue and the spores remain dormant. Alpine winters and spring thaws are familiar parts of the setting, but they do not decide which cue the assay actually sampled. The smoke treatment is the sufficient and necessary route in this case.",
"checks": {
"Q1": "FAIL",
"Q2": "FAIL",
"Q3": "PASS"
}
}

